<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rusokastro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1332">1332</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rusokastro was fought on 18 July 1332 near the fortress of Rusokastro, west of Burgas in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Ivan Alexander defeated the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andronikos-iii-palaiologos">Andronikos III Palaiologos</a> and regained towns in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> lost in previous years. It was the last major battle between Bulgaria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rusokastro.jpg" alt="Battle of Rusokastro" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Rusokastro.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
